श्रन्थित, अस्, आ, अम्, loosed, let loose; strung,
connected, bound together; hurt, injured, killed;
overcome, overpowered; delighted.

1. श्रवस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. worthy of praise,
praiseworthy, to be celebrated, (Sāy. = श्रवणीय);
(अम्), n. anything praiseworthy, fame, glory, renown.

), स्रंसितुम्, to fall, fall down, drop, slip,
slip down or off, tumble; to fall asunder; to hang
down; to go (according to Naigh.

): Pass.
स्रस्यते, Aor. अस्रंसि: Caus. स्रंसयति, &c.,
Aor. असस्रंसत्, to cause to fall or slip down;
cause to move, loosen; to move, disturb: Desid.
सिस्रंसिषते: Intens. सनीस्रस्यते, सनीस्रंस्ति.
